    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "265779cdf83e3012a1319e994c2d2fd664a8328976d41270ca3189e2ef6838e6",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast. Half-day excursion through Buenos Aires, its history and the architectural legacy of past generations: Plaza de Mayo; the typical neighbourhood of La Boca, the city’s former natural port, where a thriving Italian community, mostly of Genoese origin, settled at the end of the 19th century; Caminito, a street declared a museum, with its colourful houses; San Telmo, the historic quarter; and Puerto Madero, the newest neighbourhood, full of international restaurants.\n\nContinue to Recoleta, for decades the most prestigious neighbourhood, with its late 19th- and early 20th-century European-style buildings, its glamorous streets and its remarkable cemetery of great architectural value. The tour ends in Palermo, valued for the green spaces that form the lungs of Buenos Aires. Return to the hotel.",
